<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Hordak the Horde Dad</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;Or 5 times Hordak tried to look after someone else and 1 that someone looked after him.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;After the dust had settled and reconstruction was well underway something started to become obvious. Something utterly unexpected and frankly bizarre. But the longer peace went on for, the more difficult it became to ignore.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hordak, despite having no father figure to base his behaviour on, was paternal. Very paternal. Taking anyone that he had had even a passing responsibility for under his wing much to the growing bafflement of anyone that found themselves the target of his fatherly instincts.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>LillyLaroux (NinaWhite)</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
      <dc:subject>
        <rdf:Bag>
